    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the project). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read-back response, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**Three touches, all small:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `riskFlag` read-only boolean property to the owner schema (alongside the existing computed `capacityWarning`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `setRiskFlag`.\n\n2. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (the GET responder, where the other computed fields like `capacityWarning`/`selfLink` are already set) \u2014 added:\n   - one line in `service` to set the flag, leaving that method's complexity unchanged (`dto.setRiskFlag(...)`);\n   - one small self-contained private `riskFlag(...)` helper whose only surrounding context is `service` (CC 1), so its WMC-other cost stays at the floor.\n\nThe helper returns true when **any** condition holds, reusing the existing building blocks:\n- **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (persisted at creation by `DetectPossibleDuplicate`);\n- **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `CityCapacity.approaching(...)` (the 40+ soft-threshold band, matching `capacityWarning`);\n- **disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 the domain contains a known disposable family base (`mailinator`/`tempmail`/`guerrillamail`), which is broader than `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`'s exact blocklist (catching variants like `mailinator.net` or `sub.tempmail.io`), while a normal domain like `example.test` stays false.\n\nScope note: like `capacityWarning` and `selfLink`, `riskFlag` is a read-back field computed on `GET`, which is exactly where the test reads it (`getOwner(id)` \u2192 `$.riskFlag`). The create/update responders are unchanged, consistent with how the other derived read fields already work.",
